      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2008-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using a common denominator, \\[ \\dfrac{1}{2} + \\dfrac{2}{3} = \\dfrac{3}{6} + \\dfrac{4}{6} = \\dfrac{7}{6}. \\]\n\nThe reciprocal of \\(\\dfrac{7}{6}\\) is \\(\\dfrac{6}{7}.\\)\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
